WEBVTT

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.110
What's happening with it, Gomez?

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.880
Shyamalan is currently searching for it.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:13.820
However, it seems we
overestimated him somewhat.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.060
You mean in leaving the Ryunka to him?

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.230
Yes. I believe it was too much for him.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.700
He has nothing within him but a deep darkness.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.010
Interesting. Why not go with it?

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:35.840
Let's have a look at this "darkness" of his, Gomez.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.930
You were having a nightmare.

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:59.840
You're intelligent for an Earthling,
yet I see you let dreams bother you.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.670
Aliens don't dream?

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.370
I don't.

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.580
This world is everything, and I enjoy it.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.620
So give me some entertainment...

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.320
With the Ryunka.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:59.720
The American luxury cruise ship
the <i>Lost Bird</i> docked in Tokyo today.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:04.390
At 243 meters long and weighing in at 64,000 tons,

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.130
it surpasses Japan's
largest cruise ship, the <i>Asuka II.</i>

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:10.470
Many people have
gathered here at Harumi Wharf

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.340
to catch a glimpse of its massive shape.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.210
The <i>Lost Bird</i> belongs to PMI,
or Playmaker Industrial Company,

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:24.350
and CEO Satyajit Shyamalan will
soon invite group representatives to...

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:27.050
A profile of Satyajit Shyamalan?

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:31.320
I want to do a feature article on
him for the club's next newsletter.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:35.220
I'd like to ask for your help
as a former club member.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.730
But you could easily find
what you need on the internet...

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:44.500
She's saying she doesn't
want that perfunctory stuff.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.700
She wants "just between us"-type stuff

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.210
that only this TV station that's in
bed with Shyamalan would know.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.510
You're being awfully supportive of your junior.

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.750
It's not like you, Senior Muroto.

00:03:56.750 --> 00:04:01.220
Hey, now. I've always been attached to my juniors!

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:04.420
You think Shyamalan has
something to do with the Sawajiri incident?

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.560
Wow! How did you know?

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:14.100
Rumor has it some freelance journalist
won't quit snooping around about Sawajiri.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.270
What? Everyone knows about you?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.700
But you know, even in our
company there are a lot of people

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.410
who think the landslide story is bogus.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.380
But reporting is being restricted.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.950
We can't even fly copters into that area now.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.750
Now hold on! That's not just sketchy,
that's a blatant cover-up!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:38.120
Sure, but as things stand
we can't do anything about it.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:45.090
But if you've got no affiliation to the station,
the restrictions don't affect you, right?

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.770
I guess not. Then you'll...

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.740
I'll find out what you want.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.440
She's exactly how she seems on TV!

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.610
Don't you think so?

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:00.340
Ugh.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.650
These press restrictions have to
be because of Shyamalan's pressure.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.120
I mean, he was there!

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.620
Yeah, but I just don't think a
human being caused that disaster.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:12.960
It was like an alien's...

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.860
<i>That</i> again?!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:18.330
Please, try to think more like a journalist!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.320
We almost got murdered, you know!

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:29.640
Hey, I told you not to talk about that in public.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.480
And this story is seriously dangerous.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.180
If a high school girl delves
too deep just out of curiosity...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:38.210
It's not just curiosity!

00:05:38.210 --> 00:05:45.620
A lot of villagers died!
The truth behind that has to be reported!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.720
You're talking too loud.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:48.860
It's hereditary.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:52.290
I'm just saying I want to be very careful here.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:55.870
Huh?

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:56.670
"Inbox" "Tsutomu Senkawa" "Where are you
right now? I need your advice on something."

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:58.070
Senkawa?

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:58.490
"Inbox" "Tsutomu Senkawa" "Where are you
right now? I need your advice on something."

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.670
A date with Nakasugi?!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:03.640
N-No, it's not like that...

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:08.180
I just thought maybe we could get
together on the last day of break.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:11.510
Dude, that's what "date" means.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:13.320
You, of all people...

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.420
Huh?

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:16.090
I knew it all along.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.220
Kn-Knew what?!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.890
Your face is like an open book.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.490
Huh?

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:27.600
You and Nakasugi, eh? Glad I lived to see the day.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.270
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.570
Senkawa?

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:36.910
I'm sorry to call you here out of the blue like this.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.110
The whole week we've
been back from Sawajiri Village,

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:45.350
she's been brooding like that.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:51.620
We were so happy she'd become
stronger and could finally lead a good life,

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:56.730
but she just sits like that,
and hardly speaks anymore.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:03.360
But sometimes, she mumbles deliriously,
saying she wants to see you.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:08.440
Seeing her like that, I couldn't just do nothing.

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.910
And her grandpa said he
wanted me to cheer her up.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.780
Oh, I see.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:18.450
So now you're all worried because
you don't know where to take her?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:24.390
She says she wants to see the ocean,
but I'm no good at this stuff...

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:28.590
But getting a chance to date
her makes you happy too, right?

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:30.730
I'm telling you, it's not a date!

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.260
Fine, fine, you don't have to flip out about it.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:37.670
Let me think... How about Odaiba?

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:38.430
Huh?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.070
It's a cliché, but for a girl
it's actually pretty fun.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:46.580
O-Odaiba, huh? That could be good.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.180
Give me that.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:52.810
Your taste can't be trusted.
I'll make you the perfect plan!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:59.660
Oh, Miss Natsumi, I beg you
will favor me with your guidance.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.640
Good boy.

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:04.530
Yeah.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:08.130
I was wondering, how about Odaiba?
I know it's the standard, but...

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.170
Oh, wow! I've never been there.
I bet it'll be so much fun!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:13.300
Really?

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.270
Yeah!

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:17.540
I made us a perfect plan, so look forward to it.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:18.440
Okay.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:23.110
So, I'll meet you at 11:00 this Sunday
at the Yurikamome Shimbashi Station.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.280
Senkawa?

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.620
Thank you.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.790
Um, sure!

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:33.460
Goodnight.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:36.290
Yes!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.030
Tsutomu.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:43.170
I know, the Ryunka, right? I'll help you look.

00:08:43.170 --> 00:08:48.070
It'd be no joke if something
like that happened again.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:50.870
But this Sunday...

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.310
I want to be with her.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:01.850
Tsutomu, are you awake?

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:11.690
You've spotted the Ryunka?

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.500
From the interference of the mystery
Altan and the battle marionette,

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:20.840
I think we can assume the Ryunka
was involved in the incident.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:27.380
I'm having Irma look into the
Altan's real identity, but he said...

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:30.380
As your compatriot, I'll give you one <i>hint:</i>

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:35.080
The Ryunka possesses people.
It matures with people.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:37.390
A parasite, eh?

00:09:37.390 --> 00:09:41.360
That jibes with the new
information from our investigation.

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:45.730
There were seven survivors at Sawajiri,
not counting Tsutomu Senkawa.

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.600
One of the seven has partial amnesia.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:52.900
She was emotionally unstable
and wandering like a sleepwalker.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:53.890
And...

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:02.710
She displayed physical
abilities impossible in an Earthling.

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:08.250
I think... that Sayaka Nakasugi
must be the Ryunka's host!

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.720
As of now it's merely a high probability.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.220
You mustn't rush your conclusions, Birdy.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.760
But Sir!

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:21.460
Based on your report, a group
of pontiffs will be heading to Earth.

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:25.400
The way they do things,
they'll erase the host along with the Ryunka!

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.170
You'd let them kill an innocent Earthling?!

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:31.970
For that very reason, we need
to get proof as soon as possible

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.780
and secure the Ryunka ourselves.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:39.750
If we do that, can we eliminate
the Ryunka without killing the host?

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.920
There's no guarantee of that yet.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:43.820
Captain Megius!

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:47.920
Sayaka Nakasugi is Tsutomu
Senkawa's classmate, isn't she?

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.860
Yes.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.290
Be the one to secure the Ryunka.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:07.040
You promised, got it? Be good, just for today.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.840
Okay.

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.880
Hey, you're acting funny.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:14.620
No, I'm not.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:17.690
You seem kind of down in the mouth.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:23.860
Well yeah, being forced to facilitate
Earthling hormone rushes does turn me off.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.530
There you go, that's my Birdy.

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:27.900
Hey, wait!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.120
Senkawa!

00:11:32.070 --> 00:11:33.060
Thanks for waiting.

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:40.340
This is Nakasugi.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:46.920
Shyamalan! Right now? Sorry, but
there's no one home at the moment.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.550
Don't worry about that.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:54.890
I have something I want your advice on.
I'd like to speak with you alone.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:57.880
Yes. I'll see you in a bit, then.

00:12:18.850 --> 00:12:22.450
Here you go, two ice cream cones.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.450
Thanks.

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:26.080
Well, aren't you the little lovebirds!

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.630
This is good!

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:36.600
I had no idea there was someplace
like this right here in the city.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:40.430
That's right, I guess you
were too sick to come before.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.800
Oh, no!

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:57.950
So then I had to go in my sister's place.

00:12:57.950 --> 00:12:59.150
Poor thing.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:00.590
I know, right?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:04.230
- I'd like to meet her sometime.
- <i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:13:04.230 --> 00:13:06.830
<i>Looks like she's having fun.</i>

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.560
It's getting hot, huh?

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:12.770
Yeah.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:13.770
Thanks.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:18.670
E-Er, I didn't... l-I'm sorry!

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:22.480
What's gotten into you?! You startled me!

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:25.310
Etiquette? Oh, I see...

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:27.850
Hey, Senkawa!

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:28.850
Hmm?

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.680
I want to ride that!

00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:34.520
The Ferris wheel?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.750
<i>"Operation:</i> Tsutomu & Nakasugi's Lovey-Dovey Date"

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:39.290
Why isn't the Ferris wheel on here?!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.760
If we're in Odaiba...

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.630
I nixed the behind-closed-doors stuff.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:46.170
Can't have you going all animalistic on her.

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.770
I won't!

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:52.210
The goals of this plan are Nakasugi's
safety and spiritual refreshment.

00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:57.380
Keep that firmly in mind as you do your duty!

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:02.480
I'd like to go to the aquarium, too.
And then the Rainbow Bridge!

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:06.790
I want to go to <i>all</i> the places I've never been!

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:09.360
Yeah. Good idea!

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.160
Let's go.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.790
Sorry, Hayamiya!

00:14:15.030 --> 00:14:18.630
I see, so your granddaughter's with her friend...

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.800
She's at that age, after all.

00:14:21.800 --> 00:14:29.310
I assumed she'd be staying in bed,
unable to keep up with the changes in her.

00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.050
What are you talking about?

00:14:31.050 --> 00:14:36.150
I told you, I want to speak with you... Candidly.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:40.860
Whatever, Muroto, but can't we
at least get an air conditioner?!

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:44.330
I'm more of an environmentalist
than you might think.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.360
More importantly, look.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:50.830
This is supposed to be a training
video for PMI's young execs.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:53.940
Not everyone gets to see this.

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:57.910
Sanada got it for us through unofficial channels.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.610
Oh, here we go.

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:04.350
You're lucky. The fact that you're watching this

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.250
means you're not like the
average expendable employee.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:11.790
In other words, you were
chosen by me, the man at the top.

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.960
I guess we've been chosen.

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.890
Lucky us.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:19.390
There are only two types of people in this <i>world:</i>

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:22.970
The chosen ones, and everyone else.

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:28.240
I achieved my current status after
the will of the Universe chose me.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.610
Chosen ones eventually become the choosers,

00:15:31.610 --> 00:15:34.710
and take on the job of sifting through the riffraff.

00:15:34.710 --> 00:15:36.580
This guy's got it bad.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:37.980
Wait, look!

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:43.550
That's apparently back when
he was called a child prodigy.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.390
I've seen him somewhere before...

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:48.660
In other words,
your daughter has been chosen as well.

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:51.960
Even though she was
near-fatally injured in a car accident,

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:55.300
she was discharged from the hospital
the next day in perfect condition.

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:57.070
How do you know that?

00:15:57.070 --> 00:16:04.140
But since then, there have been
strange physical and mental changes.

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:08.580
I'm sure you must have been worried.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:12.750
Do you understand the suffering of the chosen?

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.580
The pain and loneliness...

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:18.950
"Why was I chosen?"

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:24.290
"Why am I the only one
who has to go through this?"

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:32.200
No matter how you try to forget,
you can't escape those feelings.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:36.940
You want someone to understand.
Someone to reach out to you.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:40.340
But no one will ever come.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:45.510
Because that loneliness is
the very proof of being chosen.

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:49.350
Sayaka is a truly beautiful girl.

00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:55.290
To think that behind that gentle
smile she's fighting such pain...

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:56.160
But I can...

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.160
Stop pretending to be concerned!

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:03.130
Who are you? What do you want with her?!

00:17:03.130 --> 00:17:11.570
She's beginning to change again.
From the chosen to the chooser...

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.880
I'll take her in hand.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:17.310
Don't worry, I won't treat her badly.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:20.180
I'll make sure she develops.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:23.220
It's my responsibility as a fellow chosen.

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.490
Watch it!

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:30.090
You're insane. I won't let
you lay a finger on Sayaka!

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:34.230
Is that any way to talk to the business
partner who's helping you develop marionettes?

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:38.700
You tricked me! I thought perhaps
you were here to apologize, but...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.400
Never show your face around me again!

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:44.210
I thought you'd say that.

00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:47.940
No need to worry...

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.940
You won't be seeing my face anymore.

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.780
Because you're not one of the chosen.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:03.430
I know it's here... Look!

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:04.790
Hmm?

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.900
"The site of the terrorist bombing in Taranfa.

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:12.100
Various antigovernment leaders
held a gathering in the square,

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.640
and over 4,000 civilian attendees died.

00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:20.940
Only this boy alone miraculously survived."

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:21.930
This is...

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:28.480
For real?

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:40.260
A choice has to be made about mankind.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.250
By me.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:51.510
School starts tomorrow, huh?

00:18:51.510 --> 00:18:52.670
Yeah.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:54.180
Did you finish your homework?

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:59.170
Not even close. More like,
I never wanted to do it in the first place.

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:03.410
This feels so good.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:08.260
I wonder where that boat is going?

